    "text": "A magnet of total magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is placed in a time varying magnetic field, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> where <math><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> Tesla and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.125</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The work done for reversing the direction of the magnetic moment at <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> second, is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.007</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
